-- title:
--   Local rings: if $M$ has a regular sequence $zs$ in $\mathfrak{m}$ and $ps \subseteq \mathfrak{m}$ is weakly $M$-regular, then $M/(ps)M$ has one in $\mathfrak{m}$ of length at least $|zs| - |ps|$
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$, and $M$ a nonzero finitely generated $A$-module (in the universe of $A$, as Mathlib's $\mathrm{Ext}$ requires). Let $ps$ be a weakly $M$-regular sequence of elements of $\mathfrak{m}$ and $zs$ an $M$-regular sequence of elements of $\mathfrak{m}$. Then there is an $M/(ps)M$-regular sequence $ts$ of elements of $\mathfrak{m}$ with $|zs| \le |ts| + |ps|$. A list $r_1, \dots, r_n$ of elements of $A$ is weakly $M$-regular when each $r_i$ is a nonzerodivisor on $M/(r_1, \dots, r_{i-1})M$ (Mathlib's `IsWeaklyRegular`; the last quotient may be zero), and $M$-regular (`IsRegular`) when moreover $M/(r_1, \dots, r_n)M \ne 0$. For a list $ps$, $(ps)$ is the ideal generated by its entries and $|ps|$ its length.
--
--   **Proof.** Induction on $ps$, one element $p \in \mathfrak{m}$ at a time, replacing $M$ by $M/pM$, which is finitely generated and, by Nakayama's lemma, nonzero. The step: if $M$ has a regular sequence of length $n + 1$ in $\mathfrak{m}$ and $p \in \mathfrak{m}$ is $M$-regular, then $M/pM$ has one of length $n$. By Rees' theorem (Mathlib's `ModuleCat.exists_isRegular_tfae`), the hypothesis gives $\mathrm{Ext}^i_A(A/\mathfrak{m}, M) = 0$ for $i \le n$; the long exact $\mathrm{Ext}$ sequence of $0 \to M \xrightarrow{p} M \to M/pM \to 0$ gives $\mathrm{Ext}^i_A(A/\mathfrak{m}, M/pM) = 0$ for $i < n$, and Rees' theorem turns this back into a regular sequence of length $n$ in $\mathfrak{m}$ on $M/pM$. Finally $M/(p, ps')M \cong (M/pM)/(ps')(M/pM)$, and regularity is carried by linear isomorphisms.
--
--   **Novelty.** Classical; routine formalisation.
-- source:
--   Classical commutative algebra: Rees' characterisation of regular sequences through Ext, and the long exact Ext sequence of multiplication by a regular element; see W. Bruns and J. Herzog, Cohen–Macaulay Rings, Cambridge Studies in Advanced Mathematics 39, Cambridge University Press, §1.2. C1.2 of the Diaz modulus mission. Formal proof: Diaz modulus mission, 29 October 2026 (C. Perassi).

import Mathlib

namespace DiazModulus

universe u

theorem exists_isRegular_quotient_ofList {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [Module.Finite A M] [Nontrivial M]
    (ps : List A) (hps : RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular M ps) (hpm : ∀ p ∈ ps, p ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (zs : List A) (hz : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M zs) (hzm : ∀ z ∈ zs, z ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    ∃ ts : List A, zs.length ≤ ts.length + ps.length ∧ (∀ t ∈ ts, t ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) ∧
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular (M ⧸ (Ideal.ofList ps • (⊤ : Submodule A M))) ts := by
  sorry

end DiazModulus
